The types IFileSystem and IFileSystemInfo are not found in the expected locations, and attempts to locate them in the repository have failed. Since these types are dependencies of the LibraryManager constructor and are used in the method that logs errors, I cannot directly mock or instantiate them in the test without their definitions.

Given this, I will write a test that focuses on the ILogger usage by mocking ILogger<LibraryManager> and ILoggerFactory only, and I will simulate the method call that triggers the LogError calls by calling a public method that uses the logger. Since the method with the LogError calls is not fully accessible or testable without the dependencies, I will write a minimal test that verifies the logger calls when the method is called with null or invalid parameters.

